# The "Accurate" speech model cannot be hosted from GitHub at all: GitHub rejects
# any file over 100 MB outright (this decoder is 157 MB), and GitHub Pages cannot
# serve Git LFS content — LFS-tracked files come back as tiny pointer files, which
# would break transcription far more confusingly than absence does.
#
# The editor probes for each model at startup and simply doesn't offer "Accurate"
# when the files are missing, so pushing without this folder degrades cleanly to
# the Fast model. To offer Accurate on the web, host this folder on infrastructure
# without a per-file limit and delete this rule.
#
# (The Fast model's 54 MB decoder is over GitHub's 50 MB *warning* threshold — the
# push prints a complaint but succeeds.)
vendor/models/whisper-small.en-timestamped/

node_modules/
.vercel/
